{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141bruXkgEYxnLYmcj7H9S3","type":"tool_result","content":"module github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n\ngo 1.27\n\nrequire (\nagent\nagentjob\nbotcheck\nbudget\ncli\ncloseout\ncommitter\nconfig\nconfigcmd\nconfigsrc\ncontroller\ncostblock\ncosts\ndigest\ndocscheck\neffects\nexecutor\ngithub\ngitref\ngitx\ninitcmd\nintake\njanitor\nlabels\nlimits\nmerger\nmodelauth\npool\nprgate\nprwatch\nreaper\nredact\nrepopath\nreviewer\nreviewfix\nroles\nscanner\nservecmd\nstate\ntriage\nversioncheck\nworker\nwtlock\nls: internal/tarball: No such file or directory\n9:internal/cli/               cobra command tree, global flags, slog logging; Handlers is the plug-in point\n10:internal/docscheck/         checks docs/site against the CLI commands and config keys (drift test)\n11:internal/botcheck/          tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\n12:internal/versioncheck/       tests for the version workflow in .github/workflows/version.yml (plan and tag scripts)\n13:internal/github/            GitHub client: domain types, Reader/Writer/Client, App auth, retry transport; query/ (search builder), fake/ (test double), clienttest/ (conformance suite)\n14:internal/config/            .ard/config.yaml + role directory loading into a Resolved value (pure, fs.FS in)\n15:internal/configcmd/         `ard config check` handler: prints the resolved config, returns validation errors; `--ref` checks a commit\n16:internal/configsrc/         config from origin/main: a snapshot per SHA under ~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/ (what `ard serve` reads)\n17:internal/executor/          Executor interface and plain-data job types\n18:internal/executor/local/    git worktree + host subprocess or docker run, watchdog, logs\n19:internal/agent/             Adapter interface, Spec/Result types, Registry (pure: builds argv, parses output)\n20:internal/agent/claude/      Claude Code adapter (`claude -p`, stream-json parser)\